# Copy to .env beside the checkout. Only the server reads it, and the real
# environment wins over any .env file, which is how compose passes these in
# without a mount.
#
# The music itself is a provider's: a service that answers the provider
# protocol (https://github.com/nab-os/stelly-provider) for a catalogue, and
# holds whatever account that catalogue needs.

# Where the provider listens (default http://127.0.0.1:7710).
# STELLY_PROVIDER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:7710

# The token the provider wants, if it was started with one: required when it
# listens anywhere but loopback.
# STELLY_PROVIDER_TOKEN=
